# Line-ending policy for the engram-rag repository.
#
# Forces LF line endings in the working tree and in the index for
# every source, test, doc, fixture, and config file. This pairs
# with `git config --local core.autocrlf false` (set in the repo)
# so the global Windows autocrlf=true does NOT re-convert to CRLF
# on checkout.
#
# Why explicit instead of just `* text=auto eol=lf`:
#   - The patcher in src/skills/patchSkill.ts does a byte-for-byte
#     idempotency check (`replaced === content`). Mixing LF and
#     CRLF in fixtures (some committed as LF, others as CRLF) makes
#     that check unstable across platforms. Forcing LF on all files
#     makes the check deterministic everywhere.
#   - Markdown line endings matter for diff readability, not for
#     rendering. LF makes PR diffs small and consistent.
#   - JSON is a wire format; mixing CRLF into it would break
#     anything that parses the raw bytes (Vitest does).

# Source code, tests, fixtures, docs, config: always LF.
*.md         text eol=lf
*.ts         text eol=lf
*.tsx        text eol=lf
*.js         text eol=lf
*.cjs        text eol=lf
*.mjs        text eol=lf
*.json       text eol=lf
*.jsonc      text eol=lf
*.yml        text eol=lf
*.yaml       text eol=lf
*.txt        text eol=lf
*.gitignore  text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Shell scripts and git hooks: LF only (shebangs assume LF).
*.sh         text eol=lf
*.bash       text eol=lf

# Binary assets, if any are added later, must be marked binary
# explicitly. There are none today; the policy below is a guard
# for the future and a comment for any contributor who tries to
# commit something like an image.
*.png        binary
*.jpg        binary
*.jpeg       binary
*.gif        binary
*.ico        binary
*.pdf        binary
*.zip        binary
*.gz         binary
*.tgz        binary
